pattern quicksort

problem: Sorting a list efficiently
solution:
    def quicksort(items: list[int]) -> list[int]:
        effects: none
        requires: len(items) < 10000
        if len(items) <= 1:
            return items

        pivot = items[len(items) // 2]
        left: list[int] = []
        middle: list[int] = []
        right: list[int] = []

        for item in items:
            if item < pivot:
                left.append(item)
            elif item == pivot:
                middle.append(item)
            else:
                right.append(item)

        return quicksort(left) + middle + quicksort(right)
anti-pattern: unbounded recursion without requires clause
anti-pattern: in-place mutation with side effects
